                <fr:display-uri>dhsorens-0030</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/dhsorens-0030/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="The Commitment Interface">The Commitment Interface</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    What a polynomial commitment scheme has to provide, stated precisely enough that a protocol can be proved secure against the interface rather than against a particular scheme.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>Syntax: setup, commit, open, verify — and which parameters are public.</html:li>
        <html:li>Binding, evaluation binding, and extractability; which one a <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002H/" title="The BCS Transform" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002H/" display-uri="dhsorens-002H" type="local">BCS-style</fr:link> compilation actually needs.</html:li>
        <html:li>Batch openings and homomorphism, and how much of a protocol's efficiency depends on them.</html:li>
        <html:li>Functional commitments as the generalisation, and why ArkLib separates <html:code>Commitments/Functional</html:code> from <html:code>Commitments/Ordinary</html:code>.</html:li>
        <html:li>Multilinear versus univariate interfaces, and the adapters between them.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
