              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    Constant-size proofs and a constant-time verifier, at the price of a trusted setup and a pairing-friendly curve. Still the endpoint of most <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003P/" title="Wrapping and On-Chain Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003P/" display-uri="dhsorens-003P" type="local">wrapping</fr:link> pipelines because the on-chain verifier is cheap.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The scheme and its security assumption; what the structured reference string contains.</html:li>
        <html:li>The pairing check, and why the verifier is constant-time regardless of degree.</html:li>
        <html:li>Batching and multi-point openings.</html:li>
        <html:li>Trusted setup in practice: ceremonies, updatability, and what a compromised setup permits.</html:li>
        <html:li>Why it does not scale to zkVM-sized traces, and where it survives anyway.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
